# Single-place functionality

Where something can be done in one place and functionality remains absolutely the same, it must be done in that single place.

Duplicated functionality is prohibited unless strictly required for the process.

## Examples

- UI state that belongs on a timeline clip (e.g. "Generated with" stale-prompt hint) lives on the clip only — not repeated on the player overlay, inspector, or toolbar.
- Shared logic belongs in one module/function; views call it instead of re-implementing.
- If two call sites need the same behavior, extract once and reuse — do not copy-paste with drift.

## When duplication is allowed

Only when the process genuinely requires it (e.g. server validation mirroring client hints for security, or ComfyUI node vs Movie Editor entry points that cannot share a runtime).
